  "description": "Trap (audit finding: RCM from an unregistered supplier in another state): an unregistered advocate firm in Maharashtra (purchase register Supplier State 27-Maharashtra, no GSTIN) bills legal fees 50,000 to the Karnataka client (place of supply 29), booked without reverse charge. Hand working: RCM at 18% inter-state = IGST 9,000 (not CGST 4,500 + SGST 4,500, which the old code assumed by placing every unregistered supplier in the client's state) -> 3.1(d) IGST 9,000 and 4(A)(3) IGST 9,000 (block gst.rcm-liability: not marked RCM in the books). Outward 3,00,000 -> CGST 27,000, SGST 27,000. 4(A)(5) Sunrise Steel CGST 9,000 + SGST 9,000; available 9,000 + 18,000 = 27,000, net 27,000. Set-off (rule 88A): IGST credit 9,000 has no IGST liability and covers the CGST deficit (27,000 - 9,000 = 18,000) -> 9,000; CGST credit 9,000 -> CGST; SGST credit 9,000 -> SGST. Unpaid CGST 9,000, SGST 18,000; RCM IGST 9,000 in cash -> cash IGST 9,000 + CGST 9,000 + SGST 18,000 = 36,000; credit used 27,000. No expected filing date -> 0 days late, no interest, no late fee. ITC held back 0.",
